                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "G-senjou is a VN that is often tense, and when the mystery and chases pick up, they are extremely interesting and it becomes easy to read entire segments with no realization of the time passing. However, the VN mixes romance with its thriller nature, so although the stories are sequential, if the three romance routes are played ahead of the true end as intended, the pacing does slow for these characters. Some would consider this a plus, however, I personally think they threw the pacing off considerably, and were the segments that took me the longest to read. That said, I still think each route had interesting psychological aspects, particularly Kanon's route, but that they lack payoff since the only way to reach a good end to the total story is to read the true route. Still a worthwhile, and very much entertaining (even if it did require significant suspension of belief) VN.",
